1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:03,010
(Sheldon:)building doodads with Wolowitz.

2
00:00:03,010 --> 00:00:04,710
(Sheldon:)All right.

3
00:00:04,710 --> 00:00:07,150
(Amy:)Have you considered improving
your socialization skills,

4
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:08,380
(Amy:)thus allowing you

5
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:09,980
(Amy:)to communicate more
effectively with other people?

6
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,550
(Sheldon:)Isn't that their burden?

7
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:14,550
(Sheldon:)I'm the one with something
interesting to say.

8
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:17,090
(Amy:)Fair enough, but in its essence,

9
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:18,520
(Amy:)teaching is a performance art.

10
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:20,030
(Amy:)In the classroom paradigm,

11
00:00:20,030 --> 00:00:22,730
(Amy:)the teacher has the
responsibility to communicate,

12
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:24,760
(Amy:)as well as entertain and engage.

13
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:28,170
(Sheldon:)I sense that you're trying
to slow-walk me to an epiphany.

14
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:30,070
(Sheldon:)Would you mind very much
jumping to it?

15
00:00:30,070 --> 00:00:33,570
(Amy:)Perhaps you should consider
taking acting lessons.

16
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:35,470
(Amy:)Acting lessons.

17
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,440
(Sheldon:)Interesting.

18
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:40,010
(Sheldon:)It might help
if I could act as though I care

19
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:43,750
(Sheldon:)about my students
and whether or not they learn.

20
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:47,050
(Leonard:)Penny.

21
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:50,110
Penny. Penny.

22
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:52,140
(Sheldon:)What?

23
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:55,060
You're an "actress," correct?

24
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:57,700
I'm not an "actress."

25
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:00,100
(Penny:)I'm an actress.

